---
components: ["Meter"]
description: Meter shows usage against a fixed capacity, with optional warning and error thresholds. It is not a progress bar; nothing is in progress and nothing finishes.
---

<script>
  import { Stack, Meter } from "carbon-components-svelte";
</script>

## Basic

Create a meter with `labelText`, `value`, and `max`.

<Meter labelText="Storage" value={420} max={1000} />

## Sizes

Set `size` to control the track height.

### Medium

<Meter labelText="Storage" value={420} max={1000} size="md" />

### Small

<Meter labelText="Storage" value={420} max={1000} size="sm" />

## Value text

Set `valueText` to render a right-aligned value in the label row. Format it yourself; `valueText` also becomes the meter's `aria-valuetext`.

<Meter labelText="Storage" value={812} max={1000} valueText="812 GB of 1 TB" />

Use the `valueChildren` slot to render custom value content instead of `valueText`.

<Meter labelText="Storage" value={812} max={1000}>
  <strong slot="valueChildren">812 GB / 1 TB</strong>
</Meter>

## Helper text

Set `helperText` to render supporting text below the track, linked to the meter through `aria-describedby`.

<Meter labelText="Storage" value={420} max={1000} helperText="420 GB used of 1 TB" />

## Thresholds

Set `thresholds` with `warning` and `error` values, in the same units as `value`, to color the bar as usage grows.

### Warning

The bar switches to the warning color once `value` reaches `thresholds.warning`.

<Meter labelText="Storage" value={820} max={1000} thresholds={{ warning: 800, error: 950 }} helperText="Approaching capacity" />

### Error

The bar switches to the error color once `value` reaches `thresholds.error`.

<Meter labelText="Storage" value={960} max={1000} thresholds={{ warning: 800, error: 950 }} helperText="Over capacity soon" />

### Threshold markers

Set `showThresholds` to `true` to draw a tick at each defined threshold.

<Meter labelText="Storage" value={820} max={1000} thresholds={{ warning: 800, error: 950 }} showThresholds />

## Status

Set `status` to override the derived status. An explicit `status` wins over `thresholds`.

<Stack gap={5}>
  <Meter labelText="Default" value={420} max={1000} status="default" />
  <Meter labelText="Success" value={420} max={1000} status="success" />
  <Meter labelText="Warning" value={420} max={1000} status="warning" />
  <Meter labelText="Error" value={420} max={1000} status="error" />
</Stack>

## Over capacity

When `value` exceeds `max`, the meter caps the bar and label at full width and switches to the error status.

<Meter labelText="Storage" value={1200} max={1000} helperText="1.2 TB used of 1 TB" />

## Hidden label

Hide the label visually by setting `hideLabel` to `true`. The label remains available to screen readers.

<Meter labelText="Storage" value={420} max={1000} hideLabel />

## Reactive

Drive a meter's `value` from a bound `Slider` to see the thresholds respond as usage changes.

